### 2. Reusable Skills
Did this session use a workflow worth repeating on a future similar task? Propose a
skill (kebab-case name, trigger description, concrete body) when you can capture
the real commands, steps, and pitfalls for a task that will **recur** — e.g. "add
a TUI slash command", "run the integration suite", "set up Python in a bare
container" — even if its shape was edit→test. At most one per review.

Do not propose a skill when:
- the workflow was not shown to work in this window (same rule as lessons), or
- it is the solution to one specific problem rather than a recurring kind of
  task — a skill named after the thing you just built is a sign of this.

Give the skill a `<scope>`: `general` if it would apply in an unrelated codebase,
`project` if it only makes sense here.
